  <cell width="340">
   <color r="255" g="248" b="178"><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10">
    To unlock the Cuban Dogfish in challenge or campaign games, you must earn a 1-1/2-star zoo fame rating for your zoo. 
   </font></color>
   <p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> The Cuban dogfish, Squalus cubensis, is a dogfish, a member of the family Squalidae in the order Squaliformes. It is found in the Western Atlantic from North Carolina to Florida, in the Gulf of Mexico, around Cuba, Hispaniola, southern Brazil and Argentina. It inhabits continental shelves and uppermost slopes at depths from 60 to 380 m. Its length is up to 110 cm.


   </font><p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> It is a slim, gray shark with black tips to its dorsal fins black and at the edges of its pectoral fins, its pelvic and caudal fins are white, It possess a spine at front edge of each of its two dorsal fans.


   </font><p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> It probably feeds on bottom fishes and invertebrates. The isopod parasites which commonly infest the mouth and gills of marine fish are unusually large in the Cuban dogfish. Its reproduction is ovoviviparous, with 10 pups in a litter.


   </font><p /><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10"> It is not generally utilized for food, but taken commercially for the oil and vitamins extracted from its liver.

</font></cell>
